# DMEAST — Environment Variables
#
# This file documents every environment variable the app reads.
# It contains NO REAL SECRETS — just placeholder names.
#
# REAL VALUES live in Vercel:
#   Vercel dashboard → dmeast project → Settings → Environment Variables
#
# For LOCAL development:
#   1. Copy this file to `.env.local` (which is gitignored)
#   2. Fill in real values for the keys you need
#   3. Restart `npm run dev`
#
# Vite prefix rule:
#   Variables with `VITE_` prefix are bundled into the client (visible to browsers).
#   Variables WITHOUT `VITE_` are server-only (only used inside /api/*.js).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLIENT-SIDE (VITE_*) — bundled into the React app at build time
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Firebase Web SDK config (these are intentionally public — they identify
# the project, not authorize access. Real security is via Firestore rules.)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Environment flag — "sandbox" enables sandbox.dmeastph.com behaviors,
# leave empty or set "production" for the live site.
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-SIDE — used by Vercel serverless functions in /api/
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic Claude API — used by /api/claude-rfq.js for RFQ line-item matching
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Maya payment gateway (Philippines) — used by /api/maya-*.js
# Get keys from Maya Business Manager:
#   Sandbox: https://pg-sandbox.paymaya.com
#   Production: https://pg.paymaya.com
MAYA_PUBLIC_KEY=
MAYA_SECRET_KEY=
MAYA_API_URL=https://pg-sandbox.paymaya.com

# Base URLs for payment redirects + webhook callbacks
APP_BASE_URL=https://dmeastph.com
SITE_URL=https://dmeastph.com

# Firebase Admin SDK (server-side) — used by /api/maya-webhook.js to
# update orders in Firestore. Get from Firebase Console → Project Settings →
# Service Accounts → "Generate new private key".
# NOTE: FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY must have \n preserved as literal backslash-n
# in Vercel env vars. The code does .replace(/\\n/g, '\n') at runtime.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Currently hardcoded — move to env vars in a future PR
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are still inside src/App.jsx and should be moved here over time:
#   - EmailJS service ID, template IDs, public key (around line 410)
#   - Fiuu QR image base64 data (large constant)
#   - DMEAST bank info constants
#
# Tracking issue: TODO — open one once GitHub Issues is in use.
